Z||000004||BAM-BAM||07-16-2000||12:36 AM||||  Haze, I ordered my rear KYB'S Monday morning because Summit racing pushed me back another two weeks. I payed extra for 3 day shipping and still haven't seen them. I had forgotten to mention that I was a Forum member when I ordered. I called back ten minutes later and told them about my ignorence and they told me there was nothing that they could do, the struts had already shipped. I'll give them the bennefit of the doubt this time. You'll probably be ok for a three dayer.<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>  P.S. Now my car will be on  jack stands till next weekend.<P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||07-16-2000||12:40 AM|||| Haez, one more thing, check this. I put my stock springs side by side with the Eibacks, the Eibachs are a full 1.5" shorter. I hope that's ok with you. My front suspension will be done monday. I found some bad things once I tor it all down. I need to replace the ball joints and the black rubber cushion that sits on top of the springs.<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||286SE'S||07-17-2000||02:04 PM||||The Fiero store is FAST. They are backorderd<BR>on headliners. They did call me and tell me that they would be delayed. Very nice company to deal with.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||07-17-2000||02:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BAM-BAM:<BR><B> I had forgotten to mention that I was a Forum member when I ordered. <BR>  Late, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Do we get a discount as a Forum Member??<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">  My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||5
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||07-17-2000||04:06 PM||||  Haze, I recieved my stuts today. I called the Fiero Store this morning and told them that I had payed for  three day shipping and that I hadn't recieved the struts yet and it has been a week. They were very good about it and deducted the entire shipping cost. The lady said that they had accidentaly shipped it UPS Ground. I'm pleased, at least they atoned for their mistake.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">D||||reg||12
Z||000009||ChadMan||07-17-2000||04:16 PM||||The Fiero Store is expensive, but they're a good outfit.  I ordered KYB shocks/struts for my 88 Coupe through them and they screwed up and sent me 84-87s.  When I called and told them about their mistake, they immediately sent the correct shocks/struts and a UPS call tag to send the old ones back.<P>Most businesses would have either charged my card for both sets of shocks/struts pending return of the 84-87 set, or refused to send the 88s until they got the 84-87s back, but not these guys - they knew the mistake was theirs and they trusted me not to rip them off.  That's the kind of place I want to deal with.||||reg||14
Z||000010||Alex4mula||07-17-2000||05:59 PM||||I have been ordering to the FS for about 10 years now. Have ordered more than $5K and never have had a bad experience from them. When my first Getrag failed long time ago when they were very scarce, they were the only ones who were able to get me one. Hunted two weeks for junkyards around US and got it for me. Hope they stay around for long time more...||||reg||14
Z||000011||Raydar||07-17-2000||10:36 PM||||I bought rotors, pads, mounts, dog bone, etc., etc.<BR>Took about...  ummmmm...  three days.<BR>Rather expensive, but they seem to be good folks to deal with.<BR>(Just don't let 'em talk you into CarboMet brake pads for a street car.) <P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||14
